course: dictionary
lesson: 11627
title: Aquatic: living in water
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Aquatic means living or growing in water. Its root is the Latin word aqua, which means water, so when you see aqua in a word, think of water. «The aquatic plants swayed gently in the pond.» The plants are in the pond, so aquatic must describe something that lives in water.
explain: Aquatic can also describe things that happen in or on water. «The school took us to the aquatic centre for swimming lessons.» A swimming pool is water, so an aquatic centre is a place for water sports. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: if "water" fits, you are right.
explain: The opposite of aquatic is terrestrial, which means living on land. «A fish is an aquatic animal, but a rabbit is a terrestrial animal.» Scientists use both words when they study habitats, food chains and the features that help animals survive.
fact: Aquatic means living or growing in water.
fact: «Aquatic» also means happening in or on water, as in «aquatic sports».
fact: Aquatic plants and aquatic animals live in water, such as ponds, rivers and seas.
fact: The word aquatic comes from aqua, the Latin word for water.
fact: The opposite of aquatic is terrestrial, which means living on land.
exercise: «The aquatic plants swayed in the pond.» What does aquatic mean here? | Very tall | Living on land | Blue in colour | *Living in water
exercise: Which word means the opposite of aquatic, living on land? | Wet | *Terrestrial | Floating | Deep
exercise: Which of these is an aquatic animal? | *A salmon | A camel | A rabbit | A lion
test: In «aquatic sports» like swimming, what does aquatic mean? | A sport played on a field | A sport played with a ball | *Happening in or on water | A sport done in the sky
test: Which word means living on land? | Aquatic | Watery | *Terrestrial | Floating
exam: Mia says aquatic means wet. Which is the best meaning for a science lesson? | *Living or growing in water | Dry and hot | Very wet and muddy | Happening only at night
